{"title":"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many different integers can be expressed as the sum of three distinct members of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/22547dd4dc3b95784790658cddcbd4b408ca3ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,4,7,10,13,16,19\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb3965a516614f92f9a99ebc5c7cb8e93c87010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 13 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 16 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 24 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 30 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Subtracting 10 from each number in the set, and dividing the results by 3, we obtain the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/5/945203923415882589e18c304c9f44dfc0a6dd57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{-3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />.  It is easy to see that we can get any integer between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/3683f227b0b53e6a30087db2fa3b752965ecf05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive as the sum of three elements from this set, for the total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0167e1b747a7591d1c19b5a864a4f63dbd9bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(A) } 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"59\" height=\"32\" /> integers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The set is an arithmetic sequence of numbers each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus the sum of any three numbers will be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. All the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/5714e2c2c314eb4d4b43b12db93d8b960b394074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+4+7=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80bd0709a4b2ce595c5041f3ec44d5ca0608860a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13+16+19=48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" /> are possible, totaling to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0167e1b747a7591d1c19b5a864a4f63dbd9bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(A) } 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"59\" height=\"32\" /> integers.\n</p><p>On similar lines, it can be found that the sums are arithmetic progressions (the least being 12 and the greatest being 48). By applying the formula, we get that there are 13 terms in the sequence of sums, which is our answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid b